            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the probabilities for the three possible starting points of a clockwise semicircle containing all three points.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Label the points $A,B,C$. Let $E_A$ be the event that $B$ and $C$ both lie in the clockwise semicircle starting at $A$. Each independently has probability $\\frac12$ of lying there, so\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(E_A)&=\\frac12\\times\\frac12\\\\\\Pr(E_A)&=\\frac14.\\end{align*}$$\nDefine $E_B$ and $E_C$ similarly. If all three points lie in a semicircle, exactly one of these events occurs, apart from boundary cases of probability zero. By symmetry, each event has probability $\\frac14$. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{all three lie in a semicircle})&=\\Pr(E_A)+\\Pr(E_B)+\\Pr(E_C)\\\\\\Pr(\\text{all three lie in a semicircle})&=3\\times\\frac14\\\\\\Pr(\\text{all three lie in a semicircle})&=\\frac34.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
